From: gt510 <gt510@localhost>
Subject: aperture: rotate the preview and tag captures for the camera mounting and the shell rotation

The GTK4 paintable sink did not honour the image-orientation tag pipewiresrc
derives from the libcamera orientation, so both cameras showed the raw sensor
frame. Set the paintable orientation property directly: the inverse of the
libcamera mounting rotation plus the shell output transform from
org.gnome.Mutter.DisplayConfig (phone shells rotate the whole logical output;
the preview has to be counter-rotated, in the opposite direction for a front
camera), re-applied on MonitorsChanged. Captures get the same value as their
image-orientation tag, and the stream tag from pipewiresrc is rewritten at the
source pad with the same value (the muxers keep the first tag they see), so
saved photos and videos are upright in every orientation.
APERTURE_ORIENTATION forces the total, APERTURE_DISPLAY_ROTATION the display
part. APERTURE_OPTIMAL_RATIO=4:3 makes best_mode prefer the sensor aspect.
